---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base lang="en" title="How to open a JXL file (JPEG XL) | Open JXL" description="A .jxl file is a JPEG XL image. Preview it locally in your browser, no install needed." path="/how-to-open-jxl-file/">
<section class="page-hero">
<span class="eyebrow">Guide</span>
<h1>How to open a <span class="grad">JPEG XL (.jxl)</span> file</h1>
<p class="lead">A <strong>.jxl</strong> file is a <strong>JPEG XL</strong> image - not a camera app or Java library. Here is the fastest way to see it.</p>
</section>

<section class="cta-banner">
<div class="cta-text"><strong>Fastest: preview right here</strong><p>No install. Your file never leaves this device.</p></div>
<a class="btn primary" href="/">Open the local viewer -></a>
</section>

<section class="card steps-card">
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">1</span><div><strong>Drop your file</strong><p>Drag one .jxl into the viewer, click to choose, or paste it.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">2</span><div><strong>View on-device</strong><p>Native display when supported, otherwise our local decoder fills in.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="step-n">3</span><div><strong>Save if needed</strong><p>Export JPG or PNG to share anywhere.</p></div></div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="card">
<h3>Desktop software (optional)</h3>
<p>If you prefer an app, use official builds only:</p>
<ul class="plain-list"><li><strong>ImageMagick</strong> - official builds</li><li><strong>libjxl tools</strong> (cjxl / djxl)</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="faq">
<details open><summary>What is a .jxl file?</summary><p>A still image in the JPEG XL format.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is it safe?</summary><p>Files here never leave your device; closing the tab discards them.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why won't Chrome open it?</summary><p>Native support varies by version - this site falls back to a local decoder.</p></details>
</section>
</Base>
